[ti:My Old Kentucky Home]
[ar:Stephen Foster]
[00:00.00]The sun shines bright in the old Kentucky home
[00:25.76]Tis summer, the people are gay
[00:34.64]The corn top's ripe and the meadow's in the bloom
[00:41.60]While the birds make music all the day
[00:49.04]The young folks roll on the little cabin floor
[00:55.92]All merry, all happy and bright
[01:03.68]By and by hard times comes a-knocking at the door
[01:10.72]Then my old Kentucky home, good night
